> # BEACON simulation study
> #
> # Two-tier design:
> #   1. Large Monte Carlo comparison of fast estimators.
> #   2. Smaller, computationally realistic Bayesian validation using the
> #      actual Stan implementation of BEACON.
> #
> # Default workload:
> #   - 500 repetitions per scenario for ITS, GAM and two-stage aligned NB.
> #   - 100 repetitions per scenario for BEACON-Stan.
> #   - 4 chains, 300 warm-up and 300 sampling iterations per Stan fit.
> #
> # The defaults can be changed through environment variables documented below.
> #
> # ADAPTED FOR beacon_affine_v2.stan. Changes from the v1 pipeline:
> #   * the data-generating process now includes an area-season disturbance,
> #     matching the model equation in the manuscript and giving the new
> #     area-season random effect something to recover;
> #   * the Stan data list, initial values and extracted variables follow the v2
> #     parameter names;
> #   * initial values are dispersed rather than centred on the truth, because a
> #     coverage study started at the truth is not a neutral test;
> #   * an optional long-chain subset re-fit checks that the abbreviated
> #     sampling schedule is not itself distorting calibration
> #     (BEACON_STAN_LONG_NREP).
> 
